  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
{
  "file": "Tools/Automation/agents/backups/CodingReviewer_20251009_192720/CodingReviewer_20250930_162632/CodingReviewer/CodingReviewer/AI_CODE_REVIEW_20250924.md",
  "line": 573,
  "text": "ACTION: **Adopt the Page Object Model:** This is the single biggest improvement for UI test maintenance and readability. Create separate classes for each screen to hide XCUIElement queries.",
  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
{
  "file": "Tools/Automation/agents/backups/CodingReviewer_20251009_192720/CodingReviewer_20250930_162632/CodingReviewer/CodingReviewer/AI_CODE_REVIEW_20250924.md",
  "line": 600,
  "text": "ACTION: **Focus on testing behaviors, not implementations.** Ensure tests validate the _what_ (the expected output/behavior of `debug_engine`) and not the _how_ (its internal private methods or variables). This makes tests more resilient to code refactoring.",
  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
{
  "file": "Tools/Automation/agents/backups/CodingReviewer_20251009_192720/CodingReviewer_20250930_162632/CodingReviewer/CodingReviewer/AI_CODE_REVIEW_20250924.md",
  "line": 624,
  "text": "ACTION: **Use descriptive test names.** The function name should clearly state the unit under test, the condition, and the expected result (e.g., `test<Unit>_<Condition>_<ExpectedResult>`).",
  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
{
  "file": "Tools/Automation/agents/backups/CodingReviewer_20251009_192720/CodingReviewer_20250930_162632/CodingReviewer/CodingReviewer/AI_CODE_REVIEW_20250924.md",
  "line": 675,
  "text": "ACTION: **Decouple tests from implementation details.** Rework any tests that rely on internal state, private methods, or the specific order of operations. Use only public APIs and assert on public results.",
  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
{
  "file": "Tools/Automation/agents/backups/CodingReviewer_20251009_192720/CodingReviewer_20250930_162632/CodingReviewer/CodingReviewer/AI_CODE_REVIEW_20250924.md",
  "line": 676,
  "text": "ACTION: **Consider using a mocking framework** (like OCMock or a Swift protocol-based approach) if `DebugEngine` has dependencies. This allows you to isolate the SUT and test its interactions with dependencies in a controlled way.",
  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
{
  "file": "Tools/Automation/agents/backups/CodingReviewer_20251009_192720/CodingReviewer_20250930_162632/CodingReviewer/CodingReviewer/AI_CODE_REVIEW_20250924.md",
  "line": 686,
  "text": "ACTION: **Document the \"why,\" not the \"what.\"** The test name and assertions should show _what_ is happening. Use comments to explain the _reason_ behind a complex test case.",
  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
{
  "file": "Tools/Automation/agents/backups/CodingReviewer_20251009_192720/CodingReviewer_20250930_162632/CodingReviewer/CodingReviewer/AI_CODE_REVIEW_20250924.md",
  "line": 699,
  "text": "ACTION: **Ensure Test Isolation:** Check that `setUp()` and `tearDown()` are used correctly to create a fresh test environment for each case.",
  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
{
  "file": "Tools/Automation/agents/backups/CodingReviewer_20251009_192720/CodingReviewer_20250930_162632/CodingReviewer/CodingReviewer/AI_CODE_REVIEW_20250924.md",
  "line": 700,
  "text": "ACTION: **Add Missing Tests:** Think about edge cases, error conditions, and security scenarios the AI likely missed and write those tests manually.",
  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
{
  "file": "Tools/Automation/agents/backups/CodingReviewer_20251009_192720/CodingReviewer_20250930_162632/CodingReviewer/CodingReviewer/AI_CODE_REVIEW_20250924.md",
  "line": 701,
  "text": "ACTION: **Run the Test Suite:** Execute it and see if it passes. More importantly, see if it _fails correctly_ when you intentionally break the implementation in `debug_engine.swift`. This validates that the tests are actually effective.",
  "source": "md_recommendation"
}
